    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To decrypt a ciphertext payload with a managed key, I will use AWS KMS (Key Management Service) as the external provider. AWS KMS is a managed service that makes it easy for developers and IT administrators to create and control the encryption keys used to encrypt their data. The code will import the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, and use it to interact with AWS KMS. The provider will be identifiable by the import statement for boto3 and the use of the AWS KMS client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887940601,
          "start": 1789887938492
        },
        "type": "text"
