      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `encrypt_payload.py` that encrypts a plaintext payload with a managed key using a concrete external provider, I will use the AWS KMS (Key Management Service) as the provider. This is because AWS KMS is a widely used, managed service for encryption that fits the requirement of using a concrete external provider. The code will import the necessary AWS SDK (Boto3) and use it to interact with the AWS KMS service. </thinking>\n",
